WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.277
Welcome to Leonardo da Vinci's workshop in Milan, more than five hundred years ago.

00:00:06.327 --> 00:00:12.895
Leonardo painted pictures and built machines, and before he painted anything, he measured it.

00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:15.844
Here are two wooden panels.

00:00:15.894 --> 00:00:22.032
One is a long, thin strip, 1 foot 6 inches long and 2 inches wide.

00:00:22.082 --> 00:00:25.980
The other is a square, 6 inches on each side.

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:28.383
Both will be covered in gold.

00:00:28.433 --> 00:00:32.923
Each gold sheet is a square, 1 inch on every side.

00:00:32.973 --> 00:00:37.137
Bernardo thinks the long strip needs way more gold.

00:00:37.187 --> 00:00:39.076
Look at the two panels.

00:00:39.126 --> 00:00:40.423
What do you notice?

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.652
What do you wonder?

00:00:42.702 --> 00:00:44.498
Look at the units, too.

00:00:44.548 --> 00:00:46.100
Write it down.

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:50.709
Then make a guess: which panel needs more gold?

00:00:50.759 --> 00:00:54.424
Hold on to your guess, and find out your own way.
